  "summary": "The subculture surrounding Horror Punk is intertwined with its musical output, extending the thematic elements into distinctive fashion, visual art, and live performances.",
  "description": "The subculture surrounding Horror Punk is intertwined with its musical output, extending the thematic elements into distinctive fashion, visual art, and live performances. While rooted in the sound of early punk, Horror Punk developed a unique identity through its fascination with classic monsters, gore, and Halloween aesthetics, often presented with a kitschy or darkly humorous sensibility. It influenced subsequent genres like Deathrock and Psychobilly .",
